{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/384755-cover-hard-leverage-and-alternate-idenity-anonymity","id":384755,"title":"Cover, Hard Leverage and Alternate Idenity/Anonymity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-28T20:53:04-08:00","id":384755,"title":"Cover, Hard Leverage and Alternate Idenity/Anonymity","content":"I've been reading through the D:tD core book and GMC rules and a couple of things about how Cover interacts with other systems isn't clear to me. Any thoughts appreciated...<br /> <br /> Firstly, Cover and Hard Leverage. Hard Leverage (as far as I can tell) requires that you take an action that would be a Break Point. But Demons don't have Break Points. Obviously if the particular Hard Leverage you use is grossly out of character, it's a Compromise roll, but there are some Covers for which even very cruel behaviour (violent kidnapping, torture, etc) isn't out of character at all.<br /> <br /> So: does a Demon using Hard Leverage just make a roll with the number of doors used as a penalty, with no option to remove them? Can the Demon dial up the scare factor and remove doors (as would happen if a Mortal character was hitting Break Points) and if so, should there be any associated penalty (beyond potential Compromise rolls)? The latter option seems right to me, but I'd like the perspective of people who've used the new rules.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I'm a bit unsure about how Alternate Identity, Anonymity and similar Merits work with Covers. Alternate Identity is specifically mentioned as making it harder to investigate a Cover, but how does that interact with the need for social reinforcement of a Cover? Does it count as maintaining the cover if you're mostly just keeping up the Alternate Identity? Covers are already a lot like Alternate Identities - how do you manage that interaction?<br /> <br /> I have a similar sort of question with Anonymity, which is that it seems like the requirements of maintaining your cover and the Merit are in conflict; Covers are strengthened by exactly the sorts of things you avoid using the Anonymity Merit. Does the Merit become a niche one for certain kinds of covers?<br /> <br /> How should Alternate Identity/Anonymity work mechanically? What would they look like in play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T15:33:55-08:00","id":385629,"title":"","content":"Don't know about the Hard Leverage one, so I'll leave that to someone else.<br /> <br /> Alternate Identity would apply to the cover its attached to. Let's say your primary cover is Sam a med student who does some moonlighting for less than honest people under the name of Andy. The purpose of the Andy identity would be to allow Sam to handle the work needed without it being as likely that his normal life is hindered if things go wrong (so long as they don't involve Sam being injured or captured of course.) That Sam is actually a cover identity for a demon is irrelevant as these things because these things are all things Sam does and by extension the demon does while being Sam. On the bright side demons are great liars, so the double life is gonna be a lot easier to handle than it is for a mortal.<br /> <br /> With anonymity you are working to make it harder to track you. Like one example it mentions is paying for things in cash only. Let's say you have a place you regularly go to and get lunch. The staff might if shown a picture of your cover go &quot;Oh yeah she comes by on Tuesdays for the lunch special, quiet sort, friendly enough, always paid in cash.&quot; That you exist and have a cover is stable, but its harder to track your cover because they don't have a name, address, or the like to attach to any sort of image of you.<br /> <br /> Does that help at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T03:43:32-08:00","id":386117,"title":"","content":"Like nalak42 said, if Anonimity is part of the Cover's life, then it's as aspect of it, and thus reinforces the Cover. Covers don't necessarily have to social; they can be reclusive if they want, as long as the aspects of the Cover's life are kept steady by the demon. Maybe being a crazy recluse who only comes down from his mountain cabin once a month is part of that Cover. The knowledge people have that he is, unerringly, that crazy recluse who only comes down from his mountain cabin once a month is itself a reinforcement of the Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T11:54:23-08:00","id":386540,"title":"","content":"Hard Leverage shouldn't act erroneously with the mechanics of Cover if I'm reading it correctly. The primary actor (the character abusing the victim to get what they want) takes a breaking point roll for the violent nature of the act with an appropriate penalty to that breaking point roll based on how damaging the action is to their self-image and psyche. They then make an action roll (with that penalty) applied, with a bonus applied for any tools (such as a weapon). This check is made to see if they break down the door or doors. The number of doors is based on the nature of the action (threatening to hurt as opposed to following through).<br /> <br /> For a Demon with a violent Cover (for example a CIA interrogator) this wouldn't be a compromise, so they don't take a check, and you proceed to the next step which is to roll the appropriate pool (Presence + Intimidation most likely) and on a success, a door is removed. The storyteller can decide how many doors are removed based on how ordinarily violent the action may seem as above. For a Demon with a passive Cover (for example, a young woman that works at a florist shop) this would be a compromise, so they make a compromise roll with the appropriate modifier based on how grossly out of character interrogation or violent abuse is to their Cover. Again, at Storyteller discretion, the amount of doors would be based on how violent the action itself is and again once they've rolled they'd move on to the next step which is to roll the dice pool to see if their action is successful.<br /> <br /> The storyteller may additionally decide, in the case of the violent cover, that no penalty is present since Demons do not feel like human beings feel and so their violent nature isn't going to affect them. (Normally the penalty applied to your initial integrity check is also applied to the action-roll itself as well (Presence+Intimidation+Weapon-Penalty.)<br /> <br /> Additional Thoughts: Demons only show emotion, even involuntary emotion like fear, when they want to. This means that any penalty to the action roll would come from how the character is presenting the threat to another. Even though the florist normally should be shaky, anxious and stressed - she's a Demon and doesn't have to show this. Therefore I don't think a Demon would ever take a penalty on the -action roll-, just the Compromise roll. But that is my personal opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T15:06:32-08:00","id":386724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/384755-cover-hard-leverage-and-alternate-idenity-anonymity?p=386540#post386540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additional Thoughts: Demons only show emotion, even involuntary emotion like fear, when they want to. This means that any penalty to the action roll would come from how the character is presenting the threat to another. Even though the florist normally should be shaky, anxious and stressed - she's a Demon and doesn't have to show this. Therefore I don't think a Demon would ever take a penalty on the -action roll-, just the Compromise roll. But that is my personal opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the demon has reasoned that being calm enough to do this without any issues would be suspicious. Ie you decide &quot;My hands need to be shaky, so I have my hands shaking enough that its noticeable but won't impede me too much. Probably go for barely restrained freak out level of shakey hands.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T19:02:12-08:00","id":386933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/384755-cover-hard-leverage-and-alternate-idenity-anonymity?p=386724#post386724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the demon has reasoned that being calm enough to do this without any issues would be suspicious. Ie you decide &quot;My hands need to be shaky, so I have my hands shaking enough that its noticeable but won't impede me too much. Probably go for barely restrained freak out level of shakey hands.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely right, though I would argue as a storyteller (and player) that acting afraid isn't being afraid, so wouldn't confer the same penalties. But I absolutely agree with the point you're making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T21:41:48-08:00","id":387024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/384755-cover-hard-leverage-and-alternate-idenity-anonymity?p=386933#post386933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely right, though I would argue as a storyteller (and player) that acting afraid isn't being afraid, so wouldn't confer the same penalties. But I absolutely agree with the point you're making.</div> </div> </div> </div>A solid opinion, but I was actually thinking, as a player, that willingly taking a penalty because it helps your cover might gain you some kind of benefit. Obviously, so long as its not abused. I figured if its at the right time and you can balance it right you might even be able to get a beat out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T23:05:10-08:00","id":387110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/384755-cover-hard-leverage-and-alternate-idenity-anonymity?p=387024#post387024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A solid opinion, but I was actually thinking, as a player, that willingly taking a penalty because it helps your cover might gain you some kind of benefit. Obviously, so long as its not abused. I figured if its at the right time and you can balance it right you might even be able to get a beat out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you're saying. I could definitely see that as being a good way to handle that. But, I would suggest that if you're acting panicked to maintain cover then you could potentially avoid the Cover check for Hard Leverage by imitating an the degradation of integrity through a Demon's ability to lie. Therefore, I would suggest the benefit from pretending to be terrified would be a bonus rather than a penalty to the initial Cover check for Hard Leverage.<br /> <br /> It still has room for abuse, so as a storyteller, one should be careful and remember there's more to Cover than just what an individual thinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 01-31-2015, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:55:27-08:00","id":388778,"title":"","content":"That clears it up a bunch. Much appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}